\section*{A conditional charged Penrose bound in spatial dimension at least four}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. For purely electric data in dimensions $n\geq4$, a charged upper-area inequality and Reissner--Nordstrom--Tangherlini equality classification are claimed under the specified decay and trapping conditions.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Area positivity and end preparation first put the data in the neutral companion scope. A coupled scalar system converts electric flux into a controlled energy decrease while retaining enclosure bounds; equality of that conversion reconstructs the original spacelike exterior with vanishing induced magnetic form.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
For purely electric data in dimensions $n\geq4$, a charged upper-area inequality and Reissner--Nordstrom--Tangherlini equality classification are claimed under the specified decay and trapping conditions. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
